{"causes":["The rise of the Medjay, a group of Nubian mercenaries, in ancient Egypt during the Sixth Dynasty.","The tumultuous politics of the Sixth Dynasty, which saw the rise and fall of several short-lived dynasties.","The cultural exchange and influence of Nubia on ancient Egyptian society during this period."],"effects":["The shaping of the military and administrative structures of ancient Egypt through the presence of the Medjay.","The legacy of the Medjay in the region's history, which continues to influence the politics and culture of the Nile Valley to this day.","The ongoing historical investigation into Neferka's impact, which seeks to shed light on the enigmatic figure's role in shaping the course of ancient Egyptian history."],"relationships":[{"sourceSlug":"Medjay","sourceName":"Medjay","verb":"CONTAINS","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"The Medjay were a group of Nubian mercenaries who served as soldiers and administrators in ancient Egypt during the Sixth Dynasty."},{"sourceSlug":"Sixth Dynasty","sourceName":"Sixth Dynasty","verb":"OCCURS_DURING","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"Neferka's reign took place during the tumultuous Sixth Dynasty, which saw the rise and fall of several short-lived dynasties."},{"sourceSlug":"Nubia","sourceName":"Nubia","verb":"INFLUENCES","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"The cultural exchange and influence of Nubia on ancient Egyptian society during the Sixth Dynasty had a significant impact on Neferka's reign."},{"sourceSlug":"Egypt","sourceName":"Egypt","verb":"CONTAINS","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"Neferka's historical record is largely contained within the annals of ancient Egyptian history, which provides a wealth of information about his reign and the Medjay's presence in the region."},{"sourceSlug":"African History","sourceName":"African History","verb":"PARTICIPATES_IN","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"Neferka's reign was an important part of the broader narrative of African history during the Sixth Dynasty."},{"sourceSlug":"Medieval History","sourceName":"Medieval History","verb":"OCCURS_IN","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"The historical record of Neferka's reign is largely contained within the medieval history of the Nile Valley."},{"sourceSlug":"Ancient Egyptology","sourceName":"Ancient Egyptology","verb":"TRANSMITS","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"The knowledge and understanding of Neferka's historical record are transmitted through the field of ancient Egyptology."},{"sourceSlug":"Middle Eastern History","sourceName":"Middle Eastern History","verb":"COLLABORATES_WITH","targetSlug":"Neferka","targetName":"Neferka","context":"The historical record of Neferka's reign is closely tied to the broader narrative of Middle Eastern history during the Sixth Dynasty."}],"places":[{"name":"Ancient Egypt","role":"Birthplace"},{"name":"Nubia","role":"Influence"},{"name":"The Nile Valley","role":"Legacy"}],"texts":[{"title":"Wikipedia: Neferka","type":"Reference article","slug":"neferka"}],"externalLinks":["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3874224","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neferka"],"tags":["Political Leaders","political-systems","geopolitical-linkage","cause-and-effect"],"thumbnailUrl":"","quote":"","legacySummary":"","summary":"Neferka was an ancient Egyptian pharaoh of uncertain date and affiliation — likely a ruler of either the late Old Kingdom or the First Intermediate Period (c. 2200–2050 BCE), a turbulent era of political fragmentation and decentralisation following the collapse of the 6th Dynasty and the central power of the Old Kingdom. The name Neferka (Egyptian: 'Perfect is the Ka' or 'Beautiful is the Spirit') was borne by several individuals in ancient Egyptian history, and the identification of the pharaoh Neferka requires careful attention to the specific evidence available — primarily scarabs, seal impressions, and occasional mentions in later king lists.

The Old Kingdom's collapse (c. 2180 BCE) — triggered by a combination of climate change (severe drought and reduced Nile floods), administrative overreach, rising power of provincial governors (nomarchs), and possibly volcanic activity — created the First Intermediate Period (c. 2180–2055 BCE), a time of multiple competing kingdoms and local dynasties in both Upper and Lower Egypt before the Eleventh Dynasty's Mentuhotep II reunified Egypt. The historical record for rulers in this period is fragmentary and often contradictory, making precise chronology and even the identification of individual pharaohs uncertain.

Neferka's place in Egyptian history — whether as a minor ruler of the late Old Kingdom, a local pharaoh of the First Intermediate Period, or a figure from another period entirely — illustrates the challenges historians and Egyptologists face in reconstructing the complete sequence of ancient Egyptian rulers. The Egyptian king lists (Turin Canon, Abydos King List, Saqqara King List) provide the framework for reconstructing this history, but they are incomplete, inconsistent with each other, and sometimes list figures who cannot yet be confirmed archaeologically.","subjects":["Ancient Egypt","Egyptian Pharaohs","Classical Era","First Intermediate Period","Egyptology","Ancient History","Old Kingdom","3rd Millennium BCE"],"frameworks":["STRUCTURAL_ANALYSIS"],"historicalSignificance":{"significanceScore":7,"significanceNarrative":"Neferka's reign during the Sixth Dynasty had a significant impact on the politics and culture of ancient Egypt, shaping the military and administrative structures of the region through the presence of the Medjay.","significanceCategory":"regional"},"_editLog":[]}
